ive, using https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112123.\r\nPlus other typo fixes, rewording, grammatical errors and improvements.\r\n\r\nThis combines and updates the work from #112123 with additional fixes, such as lexical and grammatical errors, typos, code example issues, more brief sentences and rewording where it makes sense.\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/91521\r\n\r\n## Why am i using #112123?\r\n\r\nBecause the original PR is so old, that while it can rebase to current master without any problems, i can't PR to their branch (i tried), so i am currently doing the backup plan of PR-ing directly to the Godot engine instead.\r\n\r\nPR-ing my changes by ignoring these is just not an option as this will create a lot of extra translation and conflict resolve work.\r\n\r\nWhat i have done is rebase #112123 to master (no conflicts), cherry-pick my changes on top and resolve all conflicts by taking AThousandShips' preferences rather than mine.\r\n\r\n### Closes:\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112123 (salvage)\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115768 (incorporated in this PR)\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120179 (incorporated in this PR)\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nAI was used to find the needles in this haystack, but was NOT used to pull them out. I wrote everything by hand and thought about my decisions. I do not use agents.\r\n\r\nI do not expect this to be merged now, right as 4.7 is about to release.","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-06-15T22:09:36Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T22:29:55Z","closed_at":"2026-06-15T22:18:35Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"0dc5770a20efb83bf90774152d51453ada51c4ee","assignee":nu